  "description": "All FOUR of UPDATE-USER-INFO's independent change tests fire in one invocation - app/cbl/COUSR02C.cbl:219-234 - which is the strongest available proof that they are four separate IF statements rather than one compound test. Each of the first name, last name, password and user type differs from the seeded USER0005 row, so each MOVE runs and each sets USR-MODIFIED-YES; the record that reaches the REWRITE therefore carries four changed spans at once, and the 80-byte image below pins every one of them together with the untouched SEC-USR-FILLER.\n\nexpectedWrites states the write itself and expectedFinalState states the resulting state. They are different assertions and this case makes both: the write list says one record was written and what it contained, and the final state says row 9 now holds it while the other nine rows are untouched. A single list could not say both, which is why the contract carries two.",
